before:
Worked example:

```javascript
function retryDelay(attempt) {
  return Number.isInteger(attempt) && attempt >= 0 && attempt < 3 ? 100 * 2 ** attempt : null;
}
console.log(retryDelay(0));
```
The returned value is 100.

after:
The first retry gets a delay of 100 milliseconds. A millisecond is one thousandth of a second.

